---
import {reviewed,requestExample} from '../lib/catalog';
const {api=null}=Astro.props;
// The current page's own tested example comes first so it loads by default.
const examples=[...(api?.example&&api.review!=='reviewed'?[api]:[]),...reviewed].map(requestExample);
const hasExample=!!api&&examples.some(e=>e.slug===api.slug);
---
<section id="playground" class="playground" data-default={api?(hasExample?api.slug:'custom'):'open-meteo'} data-docs={api?.docs}><div class="playground-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE REQUEST WORKBENCH</span><h2>Meet the data.</h2></div><span class="client-badge"><span class="status-dot"></span> Runs in your browser</span></div><p class="playground-intro">Edit a request and see what comes back. Your credentials stay in page memory and go directly to the selected API provider.</p><noscript><p class="notice">Enable JavaScript to send requests. Documentation and examples remain available below.</p></noscript><div class="workbench"><form id="request-form" class="request-editor" autocomplete="off"><div class="panel-title"><span>01 / REQUEST</span><button type="button" class="subtle-button" id="clear-request">Clear all</button></div><label class="field-label" for="request-example">Start with an example</label><select id="request-example"><option value="custom">Custom request</option>{examples.map(a=><option value={a.slug}>{a.name}</option>)}</select><div class="endpoint-label"><label class="field-label" for="request-url">Endpoint URL</label><a id="example-docs" href={api?.docs||'https://open-meteo.com/en/docs'} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Provider docs ↗</a></div><div class="endpoint-row"><label class="sr-only" for="request-method">HTTP method</label><select id="request-method">{['GET','HEAD','POST','PUT','PATCH','DELETE'].map(m=><option>{m}</option>)}</select><input id="request-url" type="url" placeholder={api&&!hasExample?`Paste an endpoint from the ${api.name} docs`:'https://api.example.com/resource'} required autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="request-destination"/></div><p id="request-destination" class="destination">Choose an HTTPS endpoint.</p><div class="editor-section"><div class="editor-section-heading"><h3>Query parameters</h3><button type="button" id="add-param" class="subtle-button">+ Add</button></div><div id="request-params" class="key-value-rows"></div></div><div class="editor-section"><h3>Authentication</h3><label class="sr-only" for="auth-type">Authentication method</label><select id="auth-type"><option value="none">No authentication</option><option value="bearer">Bearer token / OAuth access token</option><option value="header">API key in header</option><option value="query">API key in query</option><option value="basic">Basic authentication</option></select><div id="auth-fields" hidden><label id="auth-name-wrap" hidden><span class="field-label">Key name</span><input id="auth-name" placeholder="X-API-Key" autocomplete="off"/></label><label id="auth-user-wrap" hidden><span class="field-label">Username</span><input id="auth-user" autocomplete="off"/></label><label><span class="field-label" id="auth-value-label">Credential</span><input id="auth-value" type="password" placeholder="Your test credential" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"/></label><p class="field-help">Use a limited test credential. OAuth login and token refresh are handled by the provider.</p></div></div><details class="editor-section"><summary>Custom headers <span>+</span></summary><div id="request-headers" class="key-value-rows"></div><button type="button" id="add-header" class="subtle-button">+ Add header</button><p class="field-help">The browser manages Cookie, Origin, User-Agent, and other restricted headers.</p></details><div id="body-section" class="editor-section" hidden><label class="field-label" for="body-type">Request body</label><select id="body-type"><option value="json">JSON</option><option value="text">Plain text</option></select><label class="sr-only" for="request-body">Body content</label><textarea id="request-body" rows="6" spellcheck="false" placeholder={'{ "name": "Your value" }'}></textarea><label class="check mutation-check"><input type="checkbox" id="confirm-mutation"/> I intend to send this request; it may change or delete provider data.</label></div><div class="send-row"><button class="button" type="submit" id="send-request">Send request <span>↗</span></button><button class="button secondary" type="button" id="cancel-request" hidden>Cancel</button></div><p id="request-error" role="alert" class="request-error" hidden></p><p class="field-help">CORS support is required. No proxy. No saved credentials. 30-second timeout · 2 MB response limit.</p></form><div class="response-panel"><div class="panel-title"><span>02 / RESPONSE</span><button type="button" class="subtle-button" id="download-response" disabled>Download ↓</button></div><div class="response-meta" id="response-meta" role="status" aria-live="polite"><span class="status-pill">Ready when you are</span></div><div class="response-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Response view">{[['tree','Tree'],['pretty','JSON'],['table','Table'],['raw','Raw'],['headers','Headers']].map(([id,label],i)=><button type="button" role="tab" id={`tab-${id}`} data-view={id} aria-controls="response-content" aria-selected={i===0?'true':'false'} tabindex={i===0?0:-1}>{label}</button>)}</div><div id="response-content" class="response-content" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-tree" tabindex="0"><div class="response-placeholder"><span>{'{ }'}</span><h3>A little curiosity.<br/>A real response.</h3><p>Send a request to explore the response.<br/>Nothing runs automatically.</p></div></div><p class="response-footnote">Response bodies are displayed as data. Remote HTML and scripts are never executed.</p></div></div><details class="code-drawer" open><summary>Take the request with you <span>cURL / JavaScript</span></summary><div class="code-controls"><div class="segmented"><button type="button" data-code="curl" aria-pressed="true">cURL</button><button type="button" data-code="javascript" aria-pressed="false">JavaScript</button></div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="reveal-values"/> Include entered values</label><button type="button" class="button small secondary" id="copy-request">Copy code</button></div><p class="field-help">Authentication, query values, custom header values, and body content are hidden by default. Check any URL path before sharing.</p><pre class="request-code"><code id="request-code"></code></pre><p id="copy-status" role="status" class="field-help"></p></details><script id="playground-examples" type="application/json" set:html={JSON.stringify(examples).replaceAll('<','\u003c')}/></section>
<script>import '../scripts/playground.js';</script>
